Normally, the shopkeeper stays near the door, and when you're wearing a 
ring of invisibility, they stay right next to the door.  However, once
you steal stuff from the shop (by walking out a hole in the wall or
teleporting) all bets are off.  He leaves the shop and tracks you 
down looking for his money.  Normally, he may first ask you for the
money ("didn't you forget to pay?"), but in this case I'd already 
annoyed him, so he just attacked.

According to the spoilers, shopkeepers don't have the see invisible 
attribute, but they must detect you somehow.  After all, when you 
try to go into a shop while invisible, it says "Manlobbi detects
your presence." "Invisible custumers aren't welcome".  In any case,
he didn't have any trouble hitting me.


On an unrelated note, perhaps in a future release we'll get more
realistic shopkeeper behaviour.  In this case, once there are holes
dug in the wall of the shop, there's no reason for them to stay next
to the door.  They should roam around the shop.  In fact, they should
come over and ask you to pay for damages.  If there are multiple ways
out of the shop, they should just hover next to their customer.
